---
description: Compact and human reference file convention
alwaysApply: true
---
# Compact Reference Files

Use compact files first to save context.

- `.mdc` rule files are compact, model-facing rules.
- `SKILL.md` and other `.md` skill/reference files are compact, model-facing files.
- `.mdh` files are the human-readable source or counterpart files.

When both compact and human files exist, read `.mdc` or `.md` during normal agent work. Open `.mdh` only when you are explicitly editing human-facing prose or when the compact content is not enough to complete the task safely.
